---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import StageSequence from '../components/StageSequence.astro';
import ProofPoint from '../components/ProofPoint.astro';
import CTAButton from '../components/CTAButton.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Google Distributed Cloud"
  description="C-9INE helps banks, government institutions and critical-infrastructure organisations turn Google Distributed Cloud into a secure, production-ready operating platform."
>
  <!--
    This hero wording was reworked from the line Ali signed off to ship identical
    across LinkedIn, proposals, sales decks and the site (the dash was removed).
    Confirm with Ali whether that divergence is fine, or update the other channels
    to match — see docs/content-brief.md §4 (Google Distributed Cloud) for the full note.
  -->
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Google Distributed Cloud">
    <h1>Sovereignty, engineered.</h1>
    <p class="gdc-subhead">Sovereign cloud is not a location. It is an operating model.</p>
    <p class="lede">
      C-9INE helps banks, government institutions and critical-infrastructure organisations turn
      Google Distributed Cloud into a secure, production-ready operating platform, covering
      readiness and deployment, workload transformation, resilience, day-two operations and
      capability transfer.
    </p>
    <div class="page-intro__cta">
      <CTAButton href="/contact?intent=gdc-pilot">Book a GDC pilot scoping call</CTAButton>
    </div>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="gdc-explainer">
        <h2>What GDC actually is</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Google Distributed Cloud, software-only, is a Google Cloud operating model you run
          yourself: GKE-based Kubernetes, fleet management, policy and observability, deployed
          onto your own supported servers in your own data centre. Nothing ships to Google;
          nothing leaves your building unless your network design says it should.
        </p>

        <div class="gdc-explainer__diagram">
          <div class="gdc-layer gdc-layer--outer" data-reveal>
            <span class="gdc-layer__label mono-tag">Your data centre</span>
            <p class="gdc-layer__desc">Supported x86 servers · your network, storage and security</p>
            <div class="gdc-layer gdc-layer--mid" data-reveal style="transition-delay:150ms">
              <span class="gdc-layer__label mono-tag">GDC software-only</span>
              <p class="gdc-layer__desc">GKE-based Kubernetes · fleet · policy · observability · lifecycle</p>
              <div class="gdc-layer gdc-layer--inner" data-reveal style="transition-delay:300ms">
                <span class="gdc-layer__label mono-tag">Workloads</span>
                <p class="gdc-layer__desc">Containers · VMs · future specialised workloads</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="gdc-explainer__note">
          You keep control of the hardware and the data centre. Google Cloud's operating model
          runs on top of it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-raised">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <h2>The gap</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Installing Google Distributed Cloud is not the hard part. Governing it, operating it,
          recovering it, and evolving it is. That's the gap between a platform being installed
          and an organisation being ready to govern, operate, recover and evolve it. It's the gap
          C-9INE occupies.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Why now</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Most FSI estates we see run VMware, Nutanix, Hyper-V and Kubernetes side by side, each
          with its own licensing, monitoring, lifecycle and security evidence to maintain. GDC
          gives you one platform, one policy model, one fleet view, without forcing every
          workload to modernise on day one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <StageSequence stages={['Design', 'Engineer', 'Run']}>
        <article class="stage-panel">
          <span class="stage-number">01</span>
          <h3>Design: Readiness</h3>
          <p>
            We assess the estate, map it against your regulatory requirements, and define the
            target operating model before any hardware is touched.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="stage-panel">
          <span class="stage-number">02</span>
          <h3>Engineer: Deployment and workload transformation</h3>
          <p>
            GDC is software-only: GKE-based Kubernetes running on your own supported servers,
            connected or air-gapped depending on what your regulator requires. Containers and VM
            workloads move in together, in governed waves, as real regulated workloads cut over
            onto the platform.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="stage-panel">
          <span class="stage-number">03</span>
          <h3>Run: Resilience, day-two operations, capability transfer</h3>
          <p>
            Recovery, continuity and failure testing designed in, not tested for the first time
            in production. Genuine day-two operations: running the platform, not just standing it
            up. And capability transfer: your team can operate it without us. That's the most
            commercially counter-intuitive thing we say, and the most credible.
          </p>
        </article>
      </StageSequence>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-raised">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="vm-runtime">
        <h2>Not a containers-only platform</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          VM Runtime is part of GDC software-only: it lets you run traditional VM workloads
          directly on the same Kubernetes-based platform as your containers, without forcing
          every legacy application through containerisation first.
        </p>

        <div class="vm-runtime__diagram" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="vm-runtime__platform">
            <div class="vm-runtime__boxes">
              <div class="vm-runtime__col">
                <div class="vm-runtime__box" data-reveal>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="vm-runtime__icon" focusable="false">
                    <rect x="4" y="4" width="12" height="12" rx="2" />
                    <rect x="8" y="8" width="12" height="12" rx="2" />
                  </svg>
                  <span>Containers</span>
                </div>
                <div class="vm-runtime__connector" data-reveal style="transition-delay:200ms"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="vm-runtime__col">
                <div class="vm-runtime__box" data-reveal style="transition-delay:80ms">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="vm-runtime__icon" focusable="false">
                    <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="12" rx="1.5" />
                    <path d="M12,16 L12,20" />
                    <path d="M9,20 L15,20" />
                  </svg>
                  <span>VMs</span>
                </div>
                <div class="vm-runtime__connector" data-reveal style="transition-delay:280ms"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="vm-runtime__base" data-reveal style="transition-delay:360ms">GDC / Kubernetes</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="vm-runtime__stat mono-tag">
          Live today: VM Runtime deployed on GDC 1.35, running Linux VMs in production — not a
          lab environment, not a roadmap item.
        </p>

        <div class="vm-runtime__lists">
          <div>
            <h4>What you get</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>CLI, APIs and Google Cloud console management patterns</li>
              <li>VM observability through Kubernetes-native logging and policy</li>
              <li>Multiple network interfaces and VLAN-aware VM networking</li>
              <li>GPU support for VMs (Preview)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4>Why it matters</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>No premature containerisation of applications that aren't ready</li>
              <li>A real path off legacy hypervisors, not just a slogan</li>
              <li>One operations model for VMs and containers, not two</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <ProofPoint eyebrow="Proof">
        Deployed for tier-one Saudi banks and a financial regulator, in the region's strictest
        regulatory environment, including Google Cloud's own Dammam region (me-central2) and the
        Class C licence CST granted it there.
      </ProofPoint>
      <p class="proof-note mono-tag">Anonymised references, pending client approval to name.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-raised">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pilot">
        <h2>Start with a focused pilot, not a leap</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          A 4–6 week pilot makes the GDC decision tangible before you commit to a full migration
          — install and register GDC software-only on your own supported hardware, migrate a
          small representative set of VM and container workloads, and walk away with evidence,
          not promises.
        </p>

        <div class="pilot-timeline">
          <div class="pilot-timeline__line" data-reveal></div>
          <ol class="pilot-timeline__steps">
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:0ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">1</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Week 1</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">Executive alignment + target workloads</span>
            </li>
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:100ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">2</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Week 2</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">MCDC, inventory + prerequisites</span>
            </li>
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:200ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">3–4</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Weeks 3–4</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">Pilot build + workload migration</span>
            </li>
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:300ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">5</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Week 5</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">Evidence pack + business case</span>
            </li>
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:400ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">6</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Week 6</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">Production roadmap + commercials</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="pilot__cards">
          <div class="pilot__card">
            <h4>Example scope</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>4–6 weeks, subject to readiness</li>
              <li>Customer-provided supported bare-metal servers</li>
              <li>Install and register GDC software-only</li>
              <li>Migrate 1 Linux VM + 1 Windows VM</li>
              <li>Migrate 3–5 representative container workloads</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="pilot__card">
            <h4>Success criteria</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Platform installed and healthy</li>
              <li>VM Runtime enabled and validated</li>
              <li>VMs boot, connect and pass application checks</li>
              <li>Containers deploy via agreed manifests / GitOps</li>
              <li>Known gaps and prerequisites documented</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="pilot__card">
            <h4>Commercial outcome</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Confirms technical feasibility for your executives</li>
              <li>Creates a local reference and evidence pack</li>
              <li>Feeds directly into a production HLD/LLD and business case</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pilot__cta">
          <CTAButton href="/contact?intent=gdc-pilot">Book a GDC pilot scoping call</CTAButton>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .gdc-subhead {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .two-col h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .two-col .lede {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .proof-note {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .vm-runtime {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .vm-runtime h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .vm-runtime .lede {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .vm-runtime__diagram {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }

  /* The whole point of this diagram: Containers and VMs are not two
     separate things pointing at GDC, they sit inside it. So it's a
     single enclosing panel (border + tint) with the boxes resting on
     the labeled base, not a floating arrow between two shapes. */
  .vm-runtime__platform {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 26rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 5%, transparent);
    padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .vm-runtime__boxes {
    display: flex;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .vm-runtime__col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .vm-runtime__box {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    width: 9rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--gunmetal-line);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    background: var(--gunmetal);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .vm-runtime__icon {
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--aquamarine);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .vm-runtime__connector {
    width: 1px;
    height: 1.5rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 55%, transparent);
  }

  .vm-runtime__base {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: -1px;
    padding: 0.85rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 16%, var(--gunmetal));
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 35%, transparent);
    color: var(--aquamarine);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .vm-runtime__stat {
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    color: var(--aquamarine);
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .vm-runtime__lists {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .vm-runtime__lists h4 {
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .vm-runtime__lists ul {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--silver);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .vm-runtime__lists li {
    padding-left: 1rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .vm-runtime__lists li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--aquamarine);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .vm-runtime__boxes {
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .vm-runtime__box {
      width: 7.5rem;
      padding: 1rem 0.75rem;
    }

    .vm-runtime__lists {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .two-col {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }

  /* Shared reveal-on-scroll: a one-shot fade + settle for elements that
     benefit from appearing in sequence (a containment diagram, a
     platform diagram, a timeline) rather than being static text. Not
     used on ordinary copy — see google-distributed-cloud.astro's own
     notes on why the gap/why-now and proof text stay static. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    :global(html.js) [data-reveal] {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(10px);
      transition: opacity 550ms ease, transform 550ms ease;
    }

    :global(html.js) [data-reveal].is-revealed {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }

    :global(html.js) .vm-runtime__connector[data-reveal] {
      transform: scaleY(0);
      transform-origin: top;
      transition: transform 400ms ease, opacity 200ms ease;
    }

    :global(html.js) .vm-runtime__connector[data-reveal].is-revealed {
      transform: scaleY(1);
    }

    :global(html.js) .pilot-timeline__line[data-reveal] {
      transform: scaleX(0);
      transform-origin: left;
      transition: transform 900ms ease, opacity 200ms ease;
    }

    :global(html.js) .pilot-timeline__line[data-reveal].is-revealed {
      transform: scaleX(1);
    }
  }

  .gdc-explainer {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .gdc-explainer h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .gdc-explainer .lede {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .gdc-explainer__diagram {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .gdc-layer {
    border: 1px solid var(--gunmetal-line);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.25rem) clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    width: 100%;
  }

  .gdc-layer--outer {
    max-width: 30rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--silver) 4%, transparent);
  }

  .gdc-layer--mid {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 35%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 5%, transparent);
  }

  .gdc-layer--inner {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 55%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 14%, var(--gunmetal));
  }

  .gdc-layer__label {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--aquamarine);
  }

  .gdc-layer--outer > .gdc-layer__label {
    color: var(--silver);
  }

  .gdc-layer__desc {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--silver);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .gdc-layer--inner .gdc-layer__desc {
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .gdc-explainer__note {
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    color: var(--silver);
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .pilot {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .pilot h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .pilot .lede {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .pilot-timeline {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .pilot-timeline__line {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.85rem;
    left: 2.5rem;
    right: 2.5rem;
    height: 1px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 45%, transparent);
  }

  .pilot-timeline__steps {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pilot-timeline__steps li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    max-width: 8rem;
  }

  .pilot-timeline__num {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--gunmetal);
    border: 1px solid var(--aquamarine);
    color: var(--aquamarine);
  }

  .pilot-timeline__label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .pilot-timeline__desc {
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    color: var(--silver);
  }

  .pilot__cards {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .pilot__card {
    border: 1px solid var(--gunmetal-line);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .pilot__card h4 {
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .pilot__card ul {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--silver);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .pilot__card li {
    padding-left: 1rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .pilot__card li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--aquamarine);
  }

  .pilot__cta {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .pilot-timeline__line {
      display: none;
    }

    .pilot-timeline__steps {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .pilot-timeline__steps li {
      flex-direction: row;
      max-width: none;
      text-align: left;
      gap: 0.85rem;
    }

    .pilot-timeline__num {
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    .pilot__cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  const prefersReduced = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  if (!prefersReduced) {
    const revealEls = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-reveal]');
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      (entries) => {
        entries.forEach((entry) => {
          if (entry.isIntersecting) {
            entry.target.classList.add('is-revealed');
            observer.unobserve(entry.target);
          }
        });
      },
      { threshold: 0.2, rootMargin: '0px 0px -10% 0px' }
    );
    revealEls.forEach((el) => observer.observe(el));
  }
</script>
